    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Taylor Ward**, our highest-projected asset with a 71.18 score against R. V\u00e1squez. The combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a significant 19% SP skill advantage makes him an auto-start, despite a slight platoon dip. **Gleyber Torres** and **Gavin Sheets** also offer massive upside, both benefiting from highly advantageous matchups against pitchers with xERAs exceeding 4.30. **Geraldo Perdomo** remains a sneaky play; while his base projection is modest, the +19% SP skill boost against Lowder elevates him into the Strong tier (64.72), proving that matchup quality currently outweighs raw talent in our daily rotation strategy.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Matt Chapman**, who fell just short of our threshold at 44.71. While his power profile against Ben Brown is usually enticing, the combination of a lower-third batting order and a -16% SP skill penalty pushed him to the bench in favor of more efficient on-base options. We are also monitoring **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who faces an elite challenge in Skubal. Despite his 57.86 score, he remains in the lineup due to his high BvP floor and the necessity of keeping his bat active, even against a tough lefty. We are exercising caution with **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Luis Arraez** against the high-velocity looks from Brown; while their scores are serviceable, their upside is capped by the SP\u2019s delivery profile. Ensure no late weather developments impact the matchups for **Jonathan Aranda** or **Masyn Winn**, as any delay could necessitate a shift toward our bench depth. **Cal Raleigh** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on our active core to maintain our pace in the 5x5 categories.",
